{
  "duration": 60.459,
  "phrases": [
    {
      "start": 0.099,
      "end": 1.0,
      "text": "So welcome back again."
    },
    {
      "start": 1.539,
      "end": 2.599,
      "text": "Time for one more problem."
    },
    {
      "start": 3.099,
      "end": 3.839,
      "text": "Now in this problem,"
    },
    {
      "start": 4.36,
      "end": 8.159,
      "text": "a car travels at a speed of one hundred kilometers per hour"
    },
    {
      "start": 8.639,
      "end": 9.38,
      "text": "for four hours."
    },
    {
      "start": 9.96,
      "end": 12.579,
      "text": "The same distance must be covered in only two hours."
    },
    {
      "start": 13.099,
      "end": 14.279,
      "text": "What speed will the car need?"
    },
    {
      "start": 14.839,
      "end": 16.099,
      "text": "This is what we need to find."
    },
    {
      "start": 16.639,
      "end": 16.959,
      "text": "First,"
    },
    {
      "start": 17.299,
      "end": 18.859,
      "text": "we need to find the total distance."
    },
    {
      "start": 19.319,
      "end": 22.279,
      "text": "We know that distance is equal to speed multiplied by time."
    },
    {
      "start": 22.779,
      "end": 25.939,
      "text": "So distance is equal to one hundred multiplied by four."
    },
    {
      "start": 26.68,
      "end": 28.299,
      "text": "This gives us four hundred kilometers."
    },
    {
      "start": 28.779,
      "end": 30.219,
      "text": "Now this distance will remain the same."
    },
    {
      "start": 30.76,
      "end": 33.7,
      "text": "Only the time changes from four hours to two hours."
    },
    {
      "start": 34.04,
      "end": 35.139,
      "text": "Be very sure about this."
    },
    {
      "start": 35.559,
      "end": 38.259,
      "text": "Now speed is equal to distance divided by time."
    },
    {
      "start": 38.68,
      "end": 40.079,
      "text": "Putting the values in the formula,"
    },
    {
      "start": 40.439,
      "end": 48.479,
      "text": "the required speed is equal to four hundred divided by two. This gives us two hundred kilometers per hour. We can also understand it in a simple way."
    },
    {
      "start": 48.879,
      "end": 53.039,
      "text": "The time becomes half, so the speed must become double to cover the same distance."
    },
    {
      "start": 53.459,
      "end": 60.459,
      "text": "Hence, the required speed is two hundred kilometer per hour. So the final answer will be option A, two hundred kilometer per hour."
    }
  ],
